; vp ships its vite fork under the `vite` npm alias
; (`vite: npm:@voidzero-dev/vite-plus-core@0.2.x`). The lock entry therefore
; reads a 0.2.x version, which fails the peer ranges that plugins such as
; @tailwindcss/vite declare (`vite@^5.2.0 || ^6 || ^7 || ^8`). A clean
; resolution (`npm install`, and Renovate lock file maintenance, which deletes
; and regenerates the lockfile) rejects that tree with ERESOLVE. The committed
; lockfile already encodes the lenient resolution; this records the requirement
; so every clean install and the Renovate regenerate step reproduce it.
; `npm ci` still enforces lockfile integrity, so determinism is unchanged.
; See debt/2026-07-20-npm-legacy-peer-deps-vite-alias.md
legacy-peer-deps=true
